    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\"><strong>Box&nbsp;2.06</strong> Clinical criteria for the diagnosis of serrated polyposis</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "WHO Classification of Tumours Editorial Board. Digestive system tumours. Lyon (France): International Agency for Research on Cancer; 2019. (WHO classification of tumours series, 5th ed.; vol. 1). https://publications.iarc.who.int/579.",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 697.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"930\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 697.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"930\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Criterion 1:</span></strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"> At least five serrated polyps proximal to the rectum all being &ge;&nbsp;5&nbsp;mm, with two or more &ge;&nbsp;10&nbsp;mm</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 697.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"930\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Criterion 2:</span></strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"> More than 20 serrated polyps of any size distributed throughout the large bowel, with at least five proximal to the rectum</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 697.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"930\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Any histological subtype of serrated polyp/lesion (hyperplastic polyp, sessile serrated lesion without or with dysplasia, traditional serrated adenoma) is included in the final count; the polyp count is cumulative over multiple colonoscopies</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
